  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study opportunities horticulture in North C&#xF4;te d&apos;Ivoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Horticulture is a focus sector of The Netherlands in C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire. Investments in the horticulture sector have the potential to increase farmers&#x2019; incomes, contribute to food and nutrition security and bring economic development and growth. The North of C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire is economically lacking behind but the climatological circumstances to grow vegetables and fruits are better (when using irrigation). To foster the development of the horticultural sector in the north of C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire a long-term approach, knowledge transfer and capacity building are needed. Therefore a study is needed to make informed decisions.This study therefore aims for the following results:&#x2022;	Identification of business opportunities and challenges for horticulture production and marketing in north of C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire; and&#x2022;	Informing the potential extension of the Hortivoire impact cluster to the north of C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire or the establishment of a new programme/impact cluster aiming to create jobs for youth in the horticulture sector.Based on the study results decisions will be taken on possible follow-up activities, possibly funded via the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) instruments.</narrative>
  </description>
